<title>ITALY: Credito Italiano '96 parent net profit up.</title>
<headline>Credito Italiano '96 parent net profit up.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Parent net profit	  254   vs     192</p>
<p>    Gross operating profit 1,082   vs     900</p>
<p>    Ord div		   60 lire  vs    35 lire</p>
<p>    Savings share div     75 lire  vs    50 lire</p>
<p>Note - Full company name is Credito Italiano Spa.  </p>
<p>    Operating income	 3,476     vs   3,215</p>
<p>    Net interest income    2,278     vs   2,416</p>
<p>    Net bad loans	    1,182     (down 2.7 pct)</p>
<p>    Client deposits	 49,600     (up 9.6 pct)</p>
<p>    Client loans	    41,400     (up 8.5 pct)</p>
<p>    Net equity		 5,661     vs   5,510</p>
<p>Note - Credito said net commission from services rose 28.7 percent to 817 billion lire while profit from financial operations was 170 billion against a 28 billion loss in 1995.</p>
<p>Credito said the net profit of 253.9 billion lire came after factors including amortisation of 203 billion and set-asides and loan adjustments for 408 billion and extraordinary income of 255 billion deriving mainly from share portfolio adjustment.</p>
<p>It said it would continue its programme of reorganising its holdings, in particular in the next few months a new consumer credit company will become operative, Credit Fiditalia, in partnership with Societe Generale.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129450</p>
</text>
